014 QAD \\| Redzone helps manufacturers operate with Champion Pace, achieving measurable productivity, resilience, and growth in just 90 days.\n   \n\n  \n\n QAD is committed to ensuring that every employee feels they work in an environment that values their contributions, respects their unique perspectives and provides opportunities for growth regardless of background. QAD\u2019s DEI program is driving higher levels of diversity, equity and inclusion so that employees can bring their whole self to work.\n   \n\n  \n\n We are an Equal Opportunity Employer and do not discriminate against any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, sex, age, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, status as a veteran, and basis of disability or any other federal, state or local protected class.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464373793","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4464373793"},{"title":"Performance Testing","company":"Kumaran Systems","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465042026","experience":"6 Yrs","skills":[1,2,12,14,15,16,19,20,34,102],"is_walkin":false,"description":"**About Us**\n Kumaran Systems: Engineering Future\\-Ready Transformations Since 1992, Kumaran Systems has been helping enterprises bridge the past and the future, reimagining legacy systems and embracing AI\\-led possibilities. With over 34 years of delivery excellence, we specialise in re\\-engineering core applications, driving cloud transformation, and building automation\\-first, GenAI\\-enabled ecosystems across the Banking and Financial Services, Insurance, Telecom, and Automotive sectors. We help organisations not just upgrade their systems but reimagine what\u2019s possible.\n   \n\n  \n\n Why Kumaran?\n   \n\n  \n\n We blend engineering discipline with AI innovation, helping clients modernise with confidence, automate with clarity, and scale with purpose. Our global delivery model ensures agility, responsiveness, and seamless collaboration, with clients always at the heart of every engagement. At Kumaran, we don\u2019t just solve problems, we engineer future\\-ready transformations.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Title: Performance Tester (JMeter \\& NeoLoad)**\n**Experience:** \n 4\\-6 Years\n   \n\n  \n\n**Key Responsibilities**\n* Design, develop, and execute performance test scripts using Apache JMeter and NeoLoad.\n* Perform Load, Stress, Endurance, Spike, and Scalability Testing for web, mobile, and API applications.\n* Analyze performance test results and identify system bottlenecks.\n* Monitor application, server, database, and network metrics during test execution.\n* Work closely with Development, QA, DevOps, and Infrastructure teams to resolve performance issues.\n* Prepare detailed performance test reports with findings and recommendations.\n* Integrate performance testing activities into CI/CD pipelines.\n* Estimate performance testing effort and provide test planning inputs.\n\n\n**Required Skills**\n* 4\\-6 years of hands\\-on experience in Performance Testing.\n* Strong expertise in Apache JMeter and NeoLoad.\n* Experience in API Performance Testing (REST/SOAP).\n* Knowledge of workload modeling, test scenario design, and performance engineering concepts.\n* Experience with monitoring tools such as Dynatrace, AppDynamics, New Relic, Grafana, Splunk, or Prometheus.\n* Basic knowledge of SQL and database performance analysis.\n* Understanding of web technologies, application architecture, and cloud environments.\n* Experience working in Agile/Scrum teams.\n\n\n**Preferred Skills**\n* Experience with CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, Azure DevOps, or GitLab.\n* Knowledge of scripting languages like Java, Groovy, Python, or Shell scripting.\n* Exposure to cloud platforms such as AWS, Azure, or GCP.\n\n\n**Qualification**\n* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or related field.\n* Relevant performance testing certifications are an added advantage.","linkedin_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465042026","permanent_url":"https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4465042026"}]